    "answer_en": "Rhum Agricole is distilled exclusively from fresh cane juice (not molasses), resulting in herbaceous, floral, and earthy profiles. AOC Martinique requires fermentation with natural or selected yeasts on fresh must. Industrial rum uses molasses, imparting caramelized, smoky, and dense body notes. Agricole acidity is more vibrant.",
    "solution_es": "Servir a 8-10°C para resaltar acidez y frescura. Mnemotecnia: 'Jugo = Jardín' vs 'Melaza = Fábrica'.",
    "solution_en": "Serve at 8-10°C to highlight acidity and freshness. Mnemonic: 'Juice = Garden' vs 'Molasses = Factory'.",
